----- stdout -----
Generate a standalone Pina CPI crate from a Codama or Anchor IDL.

Codama IDLs are rendered natively. Anchor IDLs are normalized through Codama before the same Pina renderer runs. Use --stdin when a Codama visitor needs to pass its current, potentially transformed root node.

Usage: pina cpi [OPTIONS] --output <DIR>

Options:
      --idl <FILE>
          Codama or Anchor IDL file to render

      --stdin
          Read a normalized Codama root-node IDL from standard input

  -o, --output <DIR>
          Directory to create as the standalone CPI crate

      --mode <MODE>
          How to handle an existing output directory

          Possible values:
          - auto:      Create clients in empty destinations and update clients in existing ones
          - create:    Require an empty or nonexistent destination
          - update:    Require an existing, nonempty destination and preserve its scaffold
          - overwrite: Remove the complete destination before generating it again
          
          [default: auto]

      --no-scaffold
          Generate source files without Cargo.toml or src/lib.rs

      --npx <COMMAND>
          Executable used to normalize Anchor IDLs. Defaults to npx

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  pina cpi --idl ./target/idl/counter.json --output ./clients/counter-cpi
  pina cpi --idl ./target/idl/anchor.json --output ./clients/anchor-cpi
  cat ./idl.json | pina cpi --stdin --output ./clients/program-cpi

Anchor IDLs:
  Raw Anchor IDLs require Node.js. Pina invokes @codama/nodes-from-anchor through npx. Codama root-node IDLs do not invoke Node.js.

